1
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,200
Attention, Colombia — we interrupt
this broadcast.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:12,160
At this very moment, a revolution is
breaking out on the corner of Calle Real

3
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:14,460
and Plaza Mayor de Santa Fe.

4
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:19,200
What began as a request to borrow
a simple flower vase

5
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:23,000
from the Spaniard González Llorente's shop
has sparked the flame of freedom.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,900
We go live to the scene.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,240
Go ahead, Mariana.

8
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,400
Here there is total chaos.

9
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,920
The flower vase lies in pieces on the ground,
and the people have taken the streets.

10
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:42,800
Right now, Don José María Carbonell
is running toward the popular neighborhoods

11
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:48,200
of San Victorino to mobilize
hundreds of artisans.

12
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,300
The tension is total.

13
00:00:52,300 --> 00:01:00,000
Women led by the heroine Francisca Prieto
gather and shout slogans in the square,

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,820
while the Morales brothers fight
against the royal guards.

15
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:22,720
Viceroy Amar y Borbón watches in terror
from his balconies

16
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:32,520
as the entire crowd hurls sticks, rocks,
and stones toward the palace.

17
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:35,800
Here we have Don Antonio.

18
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,800
Don Antonio, tell us.

19
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,200
This is not just about the flower vase.

20
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:43,000
We went to ask that fellow Llorente
to lend us an ornament

21
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,500
for Antonio Villavicencio's table,
and he replied that he

22
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:47,500
lends nothing to Americans.

23
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,320
We are tired of humiliations from the peninsulares.
We will not back down.

24
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:52,400
We want an open cabildo —
down with bad government!

25
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:55,600
We want an open cabildo —
down with bad government!

26
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,200
Historic report.

27
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:02,480
The viceroyalty is at a point of no return,
and the crowd will not withdraw

28
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:05,500
until the authorities are overthrown.

29
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,000
Stay with us. We'll be right back.

